On a blank page, reconstruct:


1. one complete encoder layer;

2. one complete original decoder layer;

3. a modern pre-norm decoder-only block.

Label every arrow with a tensor shape, then compare your result with VIZ 02 and VIZ 08.

Wrap one `DecoderBlock` with token and positional embeddings, a final norm, and a vocabulary head. Overfit the model on a short periodic sequence. Check that:

- loss decreases;
- generated continuation follows the pattern;
- the causal-invariance test passes;
- removing the causal mask exposes the next target token, even if the loss on this simple period does not decrease further.
